      "mentions": [
        "Quire Structures",
        "bookbinding"
      ],
      "excerpt": "Gathering is the step where a stack of flat sheets becomes an object with a spine, and it is the first point at which a mistake becomes expensive. Four sheets folded together is a quire. Eight is comfortable. Sixteen is showing off and will not lie flat for a decade. See [[Quire Structures]]. Subjec",
