      ],
      "excerpt": "Field notes from three weeks of drawing harbour charts by lamp, which turns out to be a legible constraint rather than an affectation. A lantern gives you roughly a 300mm working circle. Everything outside it is inferred. That is a limit on how much of a chart you can hold in your head at once, and ",
      "sceneText": "",
